"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nWe headed to a restaurant we had saved in advance, determined to visit once we arrived in Geoje.  \nSince we only had a light snack for lunch, we were quite hungry and decided to arrive a little earlier than standard dinner hours.  \nYou can park right in front of the restaurant, and there is also a spacious public parking lot nearby, making parking easy and stress-free.  \n\nStepping inside, the tables were already packed with groups of people having gatherings, and right away it gave off the unmistakable vibe of a beloved local hotspot.  \nWatching folks walk in naturally and settle into their seats with ease gave us the clear impression that this is an authentic local favorite frequently visited by neighborhood residents.  \n\nSince there were two of us, we ordered the 600g Soy Sauce Marinated Duck.  \nConsidering that the 600g refers purely to the meat weight excluding vegetables, the pricing felt very reasonable and not expensive at all.  \nAfter a short wait, the duck was promptly served, and the staff grilled the meat right on the hot plate for us.  \n\nPerhaps thanks to the strong heat of the stone grill, the meat cooked to perfection in no time, and we enjoyed wrapping it in leafy greens along with the neat variety of side dishes.  \nIt was not greasy at all and had none of that gamey odor, offering the kind of delicious flavor you never get tired of and can just keep eating endlessly.  \nEating away without looking up, we were left with a slight regret, realizing that the two of us could have easily finished the 1kg portion instead.  \n\nGlancing at the locals at the neighboring table, they seasoned pros poured the complimentary garlic cloves straight onto the grill to roast together and casually finished off the meal with fried rice.  \nWatching their effortless know-how, we promised ourselves that next time we visit, we will definitely act like regulars and toss in plenty of garlic to grill together.  \n\nAs a genuine local eatery thoroughly verified by the residents, it is a wonderful spot well worth stopping by whenever you visit Geoje.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"